A-4 (Keyboard): PASS — all interactive elements tested have keyboard accessibility
  - Banner dismiss button: focusable, focus:ring-2 present
  - Delete confirm buttons: real <button> submits, not onclick
  - HTMX forms use proper submit buttons
  - Tab order is logical

  KNOWN ISSUE (noted as out-of-scope by user): delete-confirm Cancel button
  (line 447–451 of accounts.html) does not include confirm="yes" hidden input,
  so clicking Cancel re-POSTs to /accounts/{id}/delete WITHOUT confirming,
  effectively confirming rather than cancelling. Not a keyboard accessibility
  issue per se, but a UX trap. User noted this is a known follow-up.

A-5 (Visible Focus): PASS — focus:ring-2 present on all interactive elements
  Banner dismiss: focus:ring-2 focus:ring-amber-400
  Buttons: focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-indigo/red-400
  Form inputs: focus:ring-indigo-500 focus:border-indigo-500

A-6 (Structure/Landmarks): PASS — all pages tested
  - Dashboard: one <h1>, h2s for sections (after A8 fix attempt 3)
  - Accounts: one <h1>, h2s for sections
  - Transfers: one <h1>, h2s for history/flow/queue sections
  - Explorer: one <h1>
  
  Landmarks: <main>, <footer>, <header> (nav) all present in base layout.
  Heading order: h1 → h2s, no skips. PASS.

A-7 (Real Tables): PASS
  - Transfers history: real <table> with <th scope="col"> headers (line 127–138)
  - Transfers flow fallback: real <table> in <details> element (line 93–114)
  - Accounts anchor table: real <table> with headers (line 355–383)
  - Explorer data: real <table> (not tested deeply, appears structured)

